('A tariff raises domestic producer surplus by $60 million, government revenue by $20 million, and lowers consumer surplus by $105 million. Ignoring other effects, what is the strongest conclusion?', ['National surplus falls by $25 million even though protected producers gain','National surplus rises by $185 million because all three figures should be added','National surplus rises by $25 million because producer gains exceed revenue','The tariff is efficient because government receives revenue'], 'National surplus falls by $25 million even though protected producers gain','The net change is +60 +20 -105 = -25 million; distributional gains do not erase the aggregate loss.','trade_policy_evaluation'),
